From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: Win+Shift+Left/Right moves a window to the display beside it; Win+Left/Right goes on across

Windows' Win+Shift+Left/Right moves the window in front to the display beside
it, at the same place relative to the display and at its size -- maximized
stays maximized, snapped stays snapped -- going round past the last display;
and Win+Left/Right on a window already snapped to that side snaps it to the
facing half of the next display that way. Neither did anything here (GitHub
#18). Linux programs' windows are framed by the taskbar (sg_embed) and move
the same way.
---
